# The thirteen .lnk files in cases/ are the ground truth of this study: their
# exact bytes are the measurement. As they stand, none of them contains a CR or
# LF byte, so there is nothing for a line-ending conversion to rewrite, and all
# of them carry NUL bytes well inside the first 8000, so Git would classify
# them as binary on its own. This line is therefore insurance rather than a
# repair. It removes the dependency on content detection, it holds if a later
# case is added whose bytes detection reads differently, and it keeps a 298-byte
# file from being rendered as a text diff in a pull request. Integrity is
# checked properly by verify_corpus.py against SHA256SUMS, which is the part
# that would actually catch damage.
*.lnk binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Records and code keep LF on every platform, so a clone on Windows produces
# the same bytes the study was run against.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.tex text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception: it is run by Windows and wants CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

* text=auto
